@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Context
+
+`parseInstant()` in `src/index.ts` requires midnight UTC; `price()` is the single place computing a total, used by `quote` and `book`. `availability` shares `period()` with them. Bookings are stored as millisecond ranges, so the overlap check already works for any times.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** hourly rentals for items with an `hourlyPrice`, priced per hour, in quotes and bookings, integer cents.
+**Non-Goals:** hourly availability queries, discounts on hourly rentals, rules tying hourly price to daily price, opening hours.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional on `Equipment`; validated like `dailyPrice` when present (non-negative integer). Stored with the item.
+- Period parsing: times must be on the hour. A period is whole-day if both ends are midnight; otherwise it is hourly and must be under 24 hours. A period of 24h+ that is not midnight to midnight is rejected, so whole days keep their meaning. Exactly 24 hours from midnight is a whole day at the daily price.
+- Hourly pricing is `hourlyPrice * hours`, no long-rental discount (it applies to days only).
+- `availability` keeps requiring whole-day periods by passing a flag to `period()`; it still excludes items with overlapping hourly bookings.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- "Shorter than a day" is read as strictly under 24 hours; an hourly period crossing midnight is allowed.
+- An hourly price above the daily price is accepted as is; the request set no relation between them.
