@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk has to turn them away because rentals are whole days only. Customers should be able to rent by the hour.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: a non-negative integer number of euro cents, the cost of one hour of rental.
+- A rental shorter than a day (under 24 hours) that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's `hourlyPrice` times the number of hours. No long-rental discount applies.
+- An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw for such a request.
+- Whole-day rentals (midnight to midnight) are unchanged. Any other period is still rejected, including one of a day or more that is not midnight to midnight.
+- Hourly bookings take part in the no-double-booking rule like any other.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+(none)
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: Equipment registration, Period rules (whole-day periods now sit beside whole-hour periods under a day), Quote and Booking.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `Equipment` type, `addEquipment` validation, period parsing and `price`.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
+- Backward compatible: `hourlyPrice` is optional and existing calls behave as before.
+- Out of scope: `availability` still takes whole-day periods only.
